# BUILT DATA IS NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# It is release payload, published as GitHub Release assets: 2 GiB per file, no
# total cap, no bandwidth quota. Putting it in the tree instead would blow the
# ~100 MB per-file hard limit, bloat every clone forever, and defeat the reason
# the whole delivery design uses Releases. c03 alone is 71 MB of CSV twins.
#
# Rebuild it instead — that is a 7-second command and it is in the README.
data/

# Notebook output noise.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
